  "title": "SellScanScreen error status check uses unsafe type assertion instead of ApiError instanceof",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: security. Severity: P3. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. In the handleEditProductSave catch block, after calling asError(_e), the code checks for 409 status using (e as { status?: number }).status. This is an unsafe type assertion. The error is already typed as Error after asError(), and the proper pattern (used elsewhere like PaymentSetupScreen) is to check `e instanceof ApiError` which has a typed status property.",
